RFW-A includes code adapted from the Articraft-based arti-template and
articraft_data research workspaces. Original module names are retained for
source-program compatibility. See docs/migration.md and its inventory for the
import boundary and RFW-A additions. The upstream Articraft project is
https://github.com/mattzh72/articraft.

This product includes source code adapted from `cq_gears`
([github.com/meadiode/cq_gears](https://github.com/meadiode/cq_gears)),
copyright 2021 meadiode@github.

The vendored implementation lives under `sdk/gears.py` and `sdk/v0/gears.py` and is
distributed under the Apache License, Version 2.0, consistent with the
upstream license.

Third-party Python dependencies are installed from PyPI under their own
licenses, which Apache-2.0 does not cover; see THIRD_PARTY.md for the list.
Notably, the `cadquery` dependency chain includes copyleft-licensed
components: Open CASCADE Technology (LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT exception, via
the `cadquery-ocp` wheels), CasADi (LGPL-3.0-or-later) and the compiled NLopt
library (LGPL-2.1-or-later). They are consumed as unmodified, dynamically
linked packages.
